namespace Magnum {
/** @page examples-multidraw Multi Draw
@brief Various approaches for reducing CPU and GPU overhead.

@m_since_latest_{examples}
@m_keywords{MultiDraw}

@m_footernavigation

@image html multidraw.png width=400px

This example displays a scene, allowing to pick between various alternative
drawing approaches. See the example source linked below for full description of
all options.

@section examples-multidraw-usage Usage

Pass a path to a glTF file or @ref file-formats "any other supported scene format"
to the application to load it. Use the UI to toggle various options.

Controls:

-   @m_class{m-label m-default} **pointer drag** rotates the scene around
-   @m_class{m-label m-default} **scroll** or
    @m_class{m-label m-primary} **pinch** zooms in/out

By default the application starts with @ref SceneGraph rendering and a profiler
enabled, you can use various command-line options to change this, which might
be useful for example when recording profiling traces.

@code{.sh}
magnum-multidraw [--magnum-...] [-h|--help] [-I|--importer IMPORTER]
    [--draw-type TYPE] [--staging-buffers] [--shader-storage-buffers]
    [--no-profile] [--] file
@endcode

Arguments:

-   `file` --- file to load
-   `-h`, `--help` --- display this help message and exit
-   `-I`, `--importer IMPORTER` --- importer plugin to use (default:
    @relativeref{Trade,AnySceneImporter})
-   `--draw-type TYPE` --- pick a concrete draw type on startup (default:
    `SceneGraph`)
-   `--staging-buffers` --- use staging uniform buffers
-   `--shader-storage-buffers` --- use SSBOs instead of UBOs
-   `--no-profile` --- `don't enable profiler on startup`
-   `--magnum-...` --- engine-specific options (see
    @ref GL-Context-usage-command-line for details)

The `-I` / `--importer` option can be also used to pass a path to an importer
plugin binary, for example to load a custom format not known to Magnum
otherwise.

The `--draw-type` option accepts one of the following values: `SceneGraph`,
`TrivialLoop`, `DeduplicatedLoop`, `DeduplicatedLoopMeshViews`, `UboPerDraw`,
`UboBindOffset`, `UboDrawOffset`, `MultiDraw`.

@section examples-multidraw-source Source

Full source code is linked below and also available in the
[magnum-examples GitHub repository](https://github.com/mosra/magnum-examples/tree/master/src/multidraw).

-   @ref multidraw/CMakeLists.txt "CMakeLists.txt"
-   @ref multidraw/MultiDrawExample.cpp "MultiDrawExample.cpp"

The example can also build on Emscripten, in which case it embeds a glTF file
for simplicity. Edit the `resources.conf` file and point it to an actual
heavyweight `*.glb` file to make it useful.

-   @ref multidraw/multidraw.html "multidraw.html"
-   @ref multidraw/resources.conf "resources.conf"

@example multidraw/CMakeLists.txt @m_examplenavigation{examples-multidraw,multidraw/} @m_footernavigation
@example multidraw/multidraw.html @m_examplenavigation{examples-multidraw,multidraw/} @m_footernavigation
@example multidraw/MultiDrawExample.cpp @m_examplenavigation{examples-multidraw,multidraw/} @m_footernavigation
@example multidraw/resources.conf @m_examplenavigation{examples-multidraw,multidraw/} @m_footernavigation

*/
}
